-- 001_extensions — nothing to do on SQLite, and the file exists to say so.
--
-- The Postgres migration of this number installs citext and pgcrypto. SQLite has neither
-- and needs neither: its TEXT columns take a COLLATE NOCASE, and ids are generated by the
-- application rather than a database default.
--
-- The file is here rather than absent because the two dialect directories share one
-- numbering. A version that simply had no file in one of them would make "the sqlite
-- database is at 007" and "the postgres database is at 007" mean different amounts of
-- schema, and the first time somebody compared them the difference would be invisible. A
-- comment-only migration is applied, recorded, and checksummed like any other, so the two
-- sequences advance together and a genuinely missing file is still an error.
